    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7853A\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the village law and the public officers law, in relation\nto qualifications to hold the position of assistant village engineer in\nthe village of Croton-on-Hudson\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation is to remove the requirement that is\nneeded to be a resident of Westchester County in order to become an\nassistant village engineer in the Village of Croton-on-Hudson.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Section 3-300 of the village law and establishes the\nqualifications to hold the position of assistant village engineer.\n\nSection 2 amends Section 3 of the public officers law by adding a new\nsubdivision 76\n\nSection 3 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrent law establishes that when selecting a candidate for assistant\nvillage engineer in the Village of Croton-on-Hudson they need to be a\nresident of Westchester. County. This legislation will remove that\nrequirement and expand the application pool to additional applicants\nregardless of where they reside specifically for neighboring counties\nand Dutchess County.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
